<!--
  Quick Settings tile brand mark (issue #268).

  Direction change (2026-09-01, recorded in AGENTS.md #5 and issue #268): tracing
  ic_launcher_monochrome.xml's isometric illustration down to a 24dp silhouette was
  tried first and rejected on real-device evidence (unrecognizable, off-centre,
  read as amateur next to stock tiles). The app logo is a detailed illustration
  whose recognisability lives in colour/lettering/internal detail that a
  single-colour 24dp silhouette cannot carry; reducing by largest-area subpath
  kept the wrong information.

  This is a purpose-built 24dp pictogram instead, drawn from scratch under the
  owner's scoped iconography exception (AGENTS.md #5, origin #268): a
  crash-survivable-recorder canister, reduced to clean, symmetric, centred
  geometry —
    - a tall rounded-rect body (the recorder canister),
    - a thin evenOdd-style cutout band near the top (the lid/cap seam,
      same "negative-space seam" convention ic_launcher_monochrome.xml uses),
    - a small rounded tab at the base (the connector).
  Body and tab are wound clockwise and unioned under the default nonzero fill
  rule (so the tab reads as seamlessly attached, not a separate floating
  shape); the seam rectangle is wound counter-clockwise and is fully contained
  inside the body's silhouette, so it subtracts a clean gap without ever
  spilling fill outside the body's outline.

  Bounding box by construction: x 6.5-17.5 (width 11, centred on 12), y
  3.5-20.5 (height 17, centred on 12) — 6.5dp side margins and 3.5dp
  top/bottom margins, i.e. geometrically centred and symmetric left-right,
  not just eyeballed.

  Single fill, no background layer, tintable via android:fillColor overrides
  (kept white here per the QS tile contract: the system tints this icon, no
  brand colour is hardcoded).
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
